Hermes patch: the browser janitor never closes a local session while another local session of the same task is in use.
Base: ~/taffy/hermes at 74943bb889 (Oct 9, 2026). Apply: cd ~/taffy/hermes && git apply ~/taffy/patches/hermes-browser-janitor-shared-chromium.patch

Why (docs/qa/2026-10-09-school-browser.md): in a served profile (every Zip on the multiplexed gateway)
browser_exec keys its agent-browser session "<task>@<profile home>" and the browser tools key theirs
"<task>". Both drive one Bot Desktop Chromium: whichever starts first launches it, the other attaches over
CDP. On Oct 9 at 14:19:54 School's browser_exec launched Chromium, browser_steps attached at 14:20:02 and
kept working, and at 14:21:55 the janitor closed the browser_exec session for 120 s of inactivity. That
closed the Chromium the browser tools and the vault's CDP supervisor were using ("CDP supervisor ... connect
failed" five times). The same split is why the Oct 8 07:43 hub note found browser_exec and the vault fill
in different tabs. This patch keeps sibling local sessions of one task alive together; when both are idle
both are closed as before. Cloud sessions and other tasks are unaffected.
Tests: tests/tools/test_browser_janitor_siblings.py (fails before, passes after); all
tests/tools/test_browser*.py and test_bot_desktop*.py pass (753 passed, 3 skipped).

